<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal raises minimum wage 3.8 percent.</title>
<headline>Portugal raises minimum wage 3.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government on Friday raised the minimum wage by 3.85 percent to 56,700 escudos ($361) a month from January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>The increase was slightly above the three percent wage deal agreed for public sector employees for next year.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
